# v-model on Object Properties

You can bind `v-model` to properties of a reactive object. This works well for grouping related fields.

```javascript
data() {
  return {
    user: {
      firstName: '',
      lastName: '',
      address: {
        street: '',
        city: ''
      }
    }
  }
}
```

```html
<input v-model="user.firstName">
<input v-model="user.address.city">
```

Vue's reactivity handles nested objects automatically (in Vue 3, via proxies).
